    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for May 20th leans heavily on the favorable matchup against V\u00e1squez, elevating **Kyle Tucker** (78.84) and **Andy Pages** (64.85) as our primary anchors. **Kyle Tucker** is the definitive start of the day; he benefits from a highly favorable opposing SP_xERA of 4.94, which significantly boosts his expected output. **Josh Jung** also grades out exceptionally well at 64.10, largely due to a +14% park factor that compensates for a tougher matchup against Freeland. While **Josh Lowe** (62.74) hits from the bottom of the order, his dynamic platoon advantage against Civale and his elite sprint speed\u2014vital for our pursuit of the scarce SB category\u2014keep him firmly in the mix despite the lineup placement penalty.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Liam Hicks**, who ultimately sits with a score of 29.95. While he remains a depth piece, a brutal draw against Sale (xERA 2.90) and a negative platoon split stifled his efficiency, pushing him well below our 40-point threshold for active play. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Jackson Merrill** (49.49). Despite the platoon advantage, he faces a stiff test against Ohtani; his start is preserved only by our need for his dynamic presence, though he remains a high-risk candidate for a mid-game swap if his early at-bats prove unproductive. We must remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson**, as both carry sub-55 scores due to challenging SP matchups; any further decline in their situational environment could necessitate a defensive shift to protect our daily game caps.",
